+ FactId is U32
+ no-fact FactId = U32.max
+ plan-bits U8 = 127
+ plain-bit U8 = 128

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ CallForm is U32

` How a call is made. `call-truth` is the call of the function that says a value is empty,
` made to test the node's own value as a condition. `call-operand-truth` is the same call
` made on an operand of the node, and its `is-swapped` says that the operand is the right one.
` `call-list-make` is the call a list written, or the variadic tail of a call, recorded at
` the call, makes of the constructor of the empty list,
` `call-list-reserve` the call it then makes of the function that reserves room for its
` items, and `call-list-data` the call of the function that answers where the array the
` list keeps its items in holds them. `call-store-through` is the call of `[]=` on the object
` an inner index reads from, which stores what `[]=` answered for the item the inner index
` gave; it is recorded at the inner index. `call-enum-default` is the construction of an enum
` with nothing given, recorded at a node whose value a number converts to the enum from: the
` number is the place of a value among those the enum declares, counted from zero, and the
` construction answers for a number that is no value's place. None is written in the source.
` `call-item-read` is the read of an item by a pattern of a list, or of what a key holds by
` a pattern of a map, recorded at the pattern written for the item: it gives what that
` pattern is matched against, and is no call of the pattern's own. `call-task` is the body of
` a task spawned where it is recorded, which runs in a task of its own, and `call-owned-task` that
` of one an object owns, which its `close` cancels. `call-view-range` is
` a call the compiler makes of a range that indexes a view of an array or a table, recorded at
` the index: its `normalize` for a range of positions, then its `forward`. `call-replaced` is
` the read of what an index holds before an array is stored there, recorded at the index
` assigned. `call-probe` is a call a probe that compiles makes of the probes module, recorded at
` the probe in the order it makes them, and `call-probe-head` one that starts a record of it.
` `call-probe-metric`, which calls nothing, marks a probe that compiles only as a metric of the
` profile, or a stream pattern whose results the profile counts, which the emitter counts or times
` through the runtime. `call-store-setter` is the call of the setter that an assigning operator
` stores its new value through, recorded at the property it assigns beside the getter that reads it.

| call-function = 0
| call-constructor = 1
| call-method = 2
| call-operator = 3
| call-static = 4
| call-getter = 5
| call-setter = 6
| call-closure = 7
| call-this-constructor = 8
| call-converter = 9
| call-truth = 10
| call-operand-truth = 11
| call-list-make = 12
| call-list-reserve = 13
| call-list-data = 14
| call-store-through = 15
| call-enum-default = 16
| call-item-read = 17
| call-task = 18
| call-view-range = 19
| call-replaced = 20
| call-probe = 21
| call-probe-head = 22
| call-probe-metric = 23
| call-store-setter = 24
| call-list-append = 25
| call-owned-task = 26


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ spawns-task Bool
    - form CallForm

` Whether a call of a form is the body of a spawned task, owned or not.
form == .call-task || form == .call-owned-task

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ answers-node Bool
    - form CallForm

` Whether a call of a form gives the value of the node it is recorded at. The calls that test
` a value as a condition do not, nor do the calls that store through an inner index or through
` a setter, nor the construction of an enum for a number converted to it, nor the read of an
` item for a pattern, nor a task spawned, nor the calls that make a list.
form != .call-truth && form != .call-operand-truth && !made && !listed

.. made = unprobed || form == .call-probe || form == .call-probe-head || form == .call-probe-metric
.. unprobed = untasked || spawns-task(form) || form == .call-view-range || form == .call-replaced
.. untasked = stores || form == .call-enum-default || form == .call-item-read
.. stores = form == .call-store-through || form == .call-store-setter
.. listed = made-list || form == .call-list-data || form == .call-list-append
.. made-list = form == .call-list-make || form == .call-list-reserve

