────────────────────
+ do reserve-nodes
    - instance InstanceId
    - binding BindingId
    - subtree SyntaxRange

if instances.rows[instance].node-start != U32.max
    =
instances.rows[instance].binding = binding
instances.rows[instance].node-start = node-types.length as U32
instances.rows[instance].subtree = subtree
for _ in 0 .. < subtree.count
    node-types += no-type
    node-calls += no-fact
    node-conversions += no-fact
    node-conversion-tails += no-fact
    node-forces += no-fact
    node-plans += OperatorPlan.plan-none
    node-chains += ChainForm.chain-tested
    node-constants += no-fact

────────────────────
+ node-slot Index?
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId

` The dense column slot of a node in its instance's body, or nothing for a node the body did
` not reserve: the absent node, one outside the subtree, or one of an instance without a body.
|? syntax == 0 || row.node-start == U32.max || syntax < row.subtree.start || syntax >= end
    null
??
    row.node-start + syntax - row.subtree.start

.. row = instances.rows[instance]
.. end = row.subtree.start + row.subtree.count

────────────────────
+ first-call FactId
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId

if slot then node-calls[slot] else no-fact

.. slot = node-slot(instance, syntax)


────────────────────
+ first-conversion FactId
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId

if slot then node-conversions[slot] else no-fact

.. slot = node-slot(instance, syntax)

────────────────────
+ do passed-conversion FactId
    - callee InstanceId
    - reason ConversionReason
    - from TypeId
    - to TypeId

` The conversion recorded for a function of a value that a function made with no syntax of
` its own gives it, or takes from it. No fact where none was recorded.
. fact = first-passed(callee)
while fact != no-fact
    . row = conversions[fact]
    if row.reason == reason && row.from == from && row.to == to
        = fact
    fact = row.next
= no-fact

────────────────────
+ first-passed FactId
    - callee InstanceId

` The first conversion recorded for a function with no node, each leading to the next.
passed-heads[callee] ?? no-fact

────────────────────
+ do record-passed FactId
    - callee InstanceId
    - relation Relation
    - reason ConversionReason
    - converter InstanceId

` Adds the conversion of an argument a function made with no syntax of its own gives a
` function, or of the answer it takes from it, with the function that converts where one
` does. No node leads to it: the function does.
. fact = ConversionFact
    - callee
    - 0
    - relation.from
    - relation.to
    - relation.kind
    - relation.rank
    - reason
    - relation.ratio
    - converter
. id FactId = conversions.length as FactId
conversions.append(fact)
chain-fact(conversion-lasts, conversion-priors, callee, id)
conversions[id].case-index = relation.case-index
conversions[id].next = first-passed(callee)
passed-heads[callee] = id
= id

────────────────────
+ do cast-conversion FactId
    - source TypeId
    - target TypeId
    - reason ConversionReason
    - from TypeId
    - to TypeId

` The conversion recorded for the function made where a value of one function type becomes
` a value of another: of an argument the second type gives to what the first takes, or of
` what the first answers to what the second does. No fact where none was recorded.
. fact = first-cast(source, target)
while fact != no-fact
    . row = conversions[fact]
    if row.reason == reason && row.from == from && row.to == to
        = fact
    fact = row.next
= no-fact

────────────────────
+ first-cast FactId
    - source TypeId
    - target TypeId

` The first conversion recorded for two function types, each leading to the next.
cast-heads[cast-key(source, target)] ?? no-fact

────────────────────
+ do record-cast FactId
    - instance InstanceId
    - source TypeId
    - target TypeId
    - relation Relation
    - reason ConversionReason
    - converter InstanceId

` Adds a conversion the function made for two function types makes, with the function that
` converts where one does. No node leads to it: the two types do. `instance` is the one
` that first makes such a value.
. fact = ConversionFact
    - instance
    - 0
    - relation.from
    - relation.to
    - relation.kind
    - relation.rank
    - reason
    - relation.ratio
    - converter
. id FactId = conversions.length as FactId
conversions.append(fact)
chain-fact(conversion-lasts, conversion-priors, instance, id)
conversions[id].case-index = relation.case-index
conversions[id].next = first-cast(source, target)
cast-heads[cast-key(source, target)] = id
= id

────────────────────
+ do place-cast
    - source TypeId
    - target TypeId
    - instance InstanceId
    - syntax SyntaxId

` Keeps where the function made for two function types is placed, where that is not where
` a value is first made the other: at a node of an instance's module. The first place an
` instance gives is kept, and a second it gives makes the function shared. A place in a second
` instance leaves none that can be told, which the place with no instance says.
. key = cast-key(source, target)
. place = ((instance as U64) /lshift/ 32) /or/ (syntax as U64)
. known = cast-places[key]
if known == null
    cast-places[key] = place
else if (known /rshift/ 32) != (instance as U64)
    cast-places[key] = ((no-instance as U64) /lshift/ 32)
else if known != place
    shared-casts[key] = true

────────────────────
+ cast-place U64?
    - source TypeId
    - target TypeId

` Where the function made for two function types is placed, as `place-cast` kept it: the
` instance above the node. Nothing where it is placed where such a value is first made.
cast-places[cast-key(source, target)]

────────────────────
+ cast-shared Bool
    - source TypeId
    - target TypeId

` Whether the function made for two function types is placed at more than one node of the
` instance that places it, as `place-cast` kept it.
