    - syntax SyntaxId
    - first FactId
    - is-operand Bool
    - is-right Bool

` Marks the most recent call recorded at a node as the test of a value as a condition, when
` it was recorded from `first` on. `is-operand` says the value is an operand of the node and
` not the node's own, and `is-right` that it is the right operand.
. fact = latest-call(instance, syntax)
if fact != no-fact && fact >= first
    calls[fact].form = if is-operand then CallForm.call-operand-truth else CallForm.call-truth
    calls[fact].is-swapped = is-right

